  "recordedOn": "2026-09-25",
  "howRecorded": [
    "S4-lab, 25.09.2026: the official image with the compose file's shape (valkey 9 over a socket, a PostgreSQL database in UTC), ports on 127.0.0.1 only, a throwaway admin.",
    "Profiles were created through POST /api/users with an explicit createdAt (the MONTH_ROLLING anchor) and lastTrafficResetAt = the sentinel 2020-01-01, so a profile Remnawave reset is one whose lastTrafficResetAt moved.",
    "bulkAllReset: POST /api/users/bulk/all/reset-traffic, then GET /api/users/by-username/{name} for each profile of set A.",
    "scheduledRuns: nothing was called; Remnawave's own scheduler reset the profiles. Instants are on the scheduler's clock.",
    "Run 'shifted-clock': the backend was started with a lab-only preload (NODE_OPTIONS=--require) that adds processClockShiftMs to Date in every Remnawave process, so its scheduler read Monday 01.02.2027 (also the 1st) minutes after start and ran all four cron jobs within 20 minutes. Timers and PostgreSQL were not shifted: the database's CURRENT_DATE stayed the real date (databaseDate), which is why this run's MONTH_ROLLING result follows databaseDate, not the scheduler's date.",
    "Run 'zone': the backend was restarted with TZ=processTimeZone and the real clock, so the zone's 00:05 and 00:10 came within the hour."
  ],
